WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.010
- [Announcer] As an entire
nation buries its head in sand.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.630
- The idea has swept the nation.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.150
But where will we find
enough sand for everyone?

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.520
- Now, there are a lot of
weird ideas floating around

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.280
out there to do with the coronavirus.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.430
Depending on which dark corner
of the internet you read,

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.910
apparently it's anything
from a liberal hoax

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.420
to 5G-activated chemtrail smart dust.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.860
More on that one later.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.650
But while most people
aren't falling for anything

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.890
quite that ridiculous,
what is driving me nuts

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.210
are these bad arguments I keep hearing

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.110
that kinda cloak
themselves in rubbish data

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.000
and shoddy logic in order
to sound reasonable.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.880
And these arguments are dangerous because

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.990
people are falling for
them, and these can have

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:45.200
some very real and severe consequences.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.470
So may I present to you

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:51.780
The Seven Worst Coronavirus Arguments!

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.970
(somber music)

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.840
I mean sure, I get how
1%, at first glance,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.400
doesn't sound that bad.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.930
And I mean, if we could picture this

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:04.660
as some kind of creepy
COVID-19 Wheel of Fortune,

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.030
then yes, the chances of you
getting that unlucky death spin

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.620
are very unlikely.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.500
But what I think most
people don't realize is

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.920
how this risk stacks up to other things

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.833
that we consider typically dangerous.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.950
1% is the same fatality risk

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.870
as a full lifetime's worth of driving.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.820
And yet think about how
much money and effort

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.280
society has spent on seat
belts, and speed limits,

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.360
and speed cameras and so on,
trying to reduce that risk.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.970
But let's go back to our wheel.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.280
Now, people seem to be
forgetting other bad outcomes,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.640
like the risk of permanent lung damage

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.750
or a long hospital visit.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.783
Now, let's spin that wheel.

00:01:48.527 --> 00:01:51.030
(clacking)

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.100
Congratulations, you will be fine.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.290
But now it's time to pass on the wheel

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.410
to two of your closest people.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:01:59.573
Thank you for playing!

00:02:01.255 --> 00:02:03.338
(chimes)

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.560
Well, last I checked, old
people are still people.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.150
And, who knows, maybe you
even know an older person

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.203
who you don't wish a 10% or
greater chance of death on.

00:02:15.231 --> 00:02:17.960
(owl hooting)

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.760
Ah yes, so next we have this one

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.620
from the self-defeatism camp.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.076
I mean, at first glance,
I get why this seems

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:26.290
all wise and baby Yoda-ish.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.170
I mean, why worry about
what you can't control?

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.360
Except for we probably
have SOME kind of agency

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.193
over this.

00:02:35.193 --> 00:02:37.330
Like, presumably these people agree that

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.310
there's some difference between,
say, staying home right now

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:43.883
and flying Wuhan and
getting your bat soup on.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.450
But even if it is already too late,

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.420
there are still things
that we can do right now

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.580
to reduce how bad it's gonna be.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.220
Our actions over the next few weeks

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.330
can decide whether it's a
long but manageable wave

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.420
that hits hospitals, or we get
hit by some hellish tsunami

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.220
that collapses medical infrastructure

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.543
and pushes the risk of
death up for everyone.

00:03:04.424 --> 00:03:06.674
(sad horn)

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.197
So yes, a similar starting
point to the one before,

00:03:10.197 --> 00:03:13.740
but more of a doom-sayer flair.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.070
These are the folks who
also think it's too late,

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.650
but also think it's the end of
everything that we hold dear.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.040
Even the mindblowingly
horrible Spanish Flu of 1918,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.340
which infected one in
every three people on earth

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.060
and had a higher death rate

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.010
still only put a temporary
halt on economic growth,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.580
and society quickly rebounded.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:38.040
Plus, medicine has improved

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:40.723
quite a lot.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.223
So, stop being silly.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.893
(intense horn)

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.200
Oo, now this one drives me mad,

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.830
because it doesn't actually
say anything useful.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.650
The word panic is completely subjective.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.910
Like, to some people, it literally means

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.810
crying and rocking in the
fetal position in the corner.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.040
And to others, it's
how they would describe

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.230
anyone who's expending any extra energy

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.664
trying to reduce their
coronavirus risk at all.

00:04:07.664 --> 00:04:09.210
(mocking laughter)

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.940
So when you do hear someone
making this kinda statement,

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.490
make sure to ask them
which specific actions

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:17.370
qualify as panic,
according to the detailed

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.100
cost-benefit analysis they
must surely have done.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.650
Because of course, no one would ever

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.660
just say this kinda thing to virtue signal

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.903
some kind of stoic superiority.

00:04:28.829 --> 00:04:31.496
(gentle chimes)

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.350
Yes indeed, the numbers
in China are slowing down,

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:38.680
and quite spectacularly, I might add.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.700
I mean, honestly, it's a miracle.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.370
Who could possibly imagine
what could've caused

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.680
such a dramatic drop in new cases?

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.960
No, but seriously, I
understand why the idea

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.050
of having to do any kind of
draconian quarantine measures

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:53.330
sounds terrible, but we've
seen that it clearly works.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.640
So, why people would then try and argue

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.300
that we don't need to do them,

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.879
because they worked elsewhere,
when it's clearly spreading?

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:03.481
(frustrated groan)

00:05:03.481 --> 00:05:05.730
(triumphant music)

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.100
So there is this thing called time,

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.590
and we don't only care
about previous time,

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.930
we also care about upcoming time,

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.580
and what is known as the future.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.330
No but seriously, this
coronavirus is brand new,

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.710
whereas flu has been around forever,

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.670
and it's already endemic around the world.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.660
So it's really unfair to compare
those two numbers so far.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.720
And while I get that exponential growth

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.110
is very counterintuitive
and can really make us

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.940
underestimate just how fast
these numbers can grow,

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.230
the reason why this argument
made my number one spot

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.010
is because it's as absurd as if

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:41.810
you're walking down the street

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:45.390
and you notice a bomb drop
out of a plane over your head.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.850
And you're like, "Guys,
quick, take cover!"

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:50.277
And your friend's like,
"Oh shut up your whining,

00:05:50.277 --> 00:05:51.967
"it's not killed anyone yet."

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.020
So there ya have it.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.200
These are the seven worst
arguments I've heard.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.640
And it's very important we
counter these when we hear them,

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:04.640
because coronavirus is kind of
a self-unfulfilling prophecy.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.950
The more we downplay
it, the worse it'll get.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:12.780
But if we take it seriously,
we can actually beat it.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.410
So yeah, I guess we
really do just have to do

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:17.100
this annoying social
distancing thing right now,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.970
because it is the only weapon we have

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.370
to fight against this damn virus.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:24.820
And it's kinda weird that
the most social thing

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:27.800
we can be doing is to stay
the hell away from each other.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.970
And on that note, time to
revisit that 5G chemtrail story

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.820
I came across on a very dark spiral

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:35.740
I went down on Facebook.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.000
Don't ask about it.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.840
I decided to bring it
to life a little more,

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.820
which is I guess what happens

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:46.403
when you don't leave
your house for a week.

